<article class="env-lemma" id="08JB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08JB">Lemma <span data-tag="08JB">21.35.3</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $K, L$ be objects of $D(\mathcal{O})$. The construction of $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (K, L)$ commutes with restrictions, i.e., for every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ we have $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (K|_ U, L|_ U) = R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (K, L)|_ U$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear from the construction and Lemma <a href="/tag/08FI" data-tag="08FI">21.20.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>